WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.590
The First Purge aims to answer a lot of the
major questions that were posed by the original

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.590
trilogy.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.620
What kind of economic and social decline might
lead to such a vicious event in the first

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.620
place?

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.990
What nefarious political underpinnings could
assure that the so-called Experiment would

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:14.990
succeed?

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.690
If we thought the New Founding Fathers of
America were depraved before, we hadn't seen

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.940
anything yet.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.320
Even so, The First Purge still leaves quite
a few stones unturned.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.740
Here are some of the biggest questions left
unanswered by the film.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.690
Consider yourself warned, there are spoilers
ahead.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.690
Tactical training

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.600
Dmitri might lead a life of crime, but he
also has a lot of talents.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.800
He handles himself quite well against the
special ops-type forces on the ground during

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.410
the Experiment and has obviously been trained.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.320
Everything from marksmanship to martial arts
to tactical wartime skills for scouring buildings

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.460
under siege and planting explosives is in
his skillset.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.450
Where he learned all of these things is something
of a mystery.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.649
There's a vague mention of his combat experience
when he and his team of street soldiers recognize

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:59.570
a mercenary symbol tattooed on their foes'
lifeless bodies, but that's pretty much the

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.620
whole story about his ultra-convenient capabilities.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.070
How he manages to be not only as good as this
gaggle of hired guns storming the city, but

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.350
good enough to defeat a dozen-plus of them
at once, is simply left to suspension of disbelief.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.729
Experimental controls

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:18.810
The NFFA's spokesman and Experiment "architect"
Dr. Updale are publicly working together on

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.479
the first Purge and seem to be on the same
team.

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:24.600
But behind the scenes, their interests differ
significantly.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.720
She's only in it to prove her point that people
need to exercise some lawlessness once a year

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.939
to function properly as a society.

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:34.950
But he wants this to work and catch on because
it'll ensure the continued rise of his new

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.039
political party.

00:01:36.039 --> 00:01:38.569
"This country needs for this to work."

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:43.060
Once he starts sending in hit squads to increase
the body count, she realizes she has no power

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.060
over the Purge.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.359
Dr. Updale often describes the Experiment
as an exercise in psychology, but her lack

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:52.679
of actual oversight or physical control undermines
that idea right away.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:57.210
Is she purposely dense about the true nature
of the night and blindly trusting of the NFFA,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.310
or does she actually believe this is how to
run a controlled behavioral experiment?

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:05.549
In either case, her collegiate credentials
really need to be reviewed.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:06.919
Lambs to slaughter

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:10.110
The NFFA isn't satisfied until the bloodshed
begins.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:14.610
They believe the best way to reduce unemployment
and poverty is to let those poor people take

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.700
themselves out.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.060
What's not clear, though, is why it takes
graphic violence to make the Experiment a

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.580
bankable success where the public is concerned.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.640
The NFFA's spokesman believes that without
a bunch of bloodshed, the organization won't

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.300
be able to expand the Purge into a national
event because it won't be attractive to outsiders.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.200
The scenes of cultural unrest seem to show
the exact opposite, though people are marching

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.980
for better treatment, not to maim one another
in the streets.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.030
So, wouldn't financial crimes be more attractive
to them?

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:42.640
Why is violence such a selling point to the
public?

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.460
You'd think seeing scenes of so much bloodshed
might make people wary of having the Purge

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.090
reach their own neighborhoods.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.340
Wouldn't it make more sense to aim for some
of the nation's other low-income areas for

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.400
expansion first?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.430
Blood money

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.710
A surprising number of people agree to stay
in Staten Island during the Experiment, despite

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.660
the possibility that they might fall victim
to whatever untold madness lies ahead.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:08.430
Part of the reason is that everyone is promised
$5,000 if they stay put, with even more compensation

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.060
for those who actually go out and participate
in the ruckus.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:15.230
But a lot of those people do perish, and it's
not clear what will become of their earnings.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.880
If Purge participants go down, do their loved
ones still get their money?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.210
Do people who don't plan to purge, but end
up doing so, get paid as well?

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.740
For that matter, does anyone actually get
paid in the end, or is that all just another

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.850
one of the NFFA's lies meant to raise the
body count?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.930
And speaking of the NFFA's trickery, what
happens to all the mercenaries and drones

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.010
they called in to raise the stakes in the
first Purge anyway?

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.240
Does the public's own thirst for violence
render them unnecessary later on, or is the

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.620
party caught cheating their way into a bigger
death toll and forced to do away with them?

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.620
Enemy unmasked

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.600
Dr. Updale puts a pretty face on the Experiment
and presents the concept as one of societal

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.280
self-betterment.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.260
In her mind, if people can live and let die
a little every now and then, they'll be better

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.350
citizens overall.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.990
"What have I done?"

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:02.430
The NFFA sees it differently, of course; if
they can push this Purge process far enough,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.510
they can essentially exterminate enough of
the underprivileged population to re-grow

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.820
the economy without openly resorting to government-sponsored
genocide.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:14.990
Naturally, that's not the NFFA's public posturing,
but does the party ever lift the veil on what

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:17.699
they're really trying to accomplish as things
move forward?

00:04:17.699 --> 00:04:21.819
It would certainly make sense that they do,
given the racially suggestive diatribe of

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:24.400
the "Polite Leader" in the original Purge
film.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.099
If not, it's also unclear how they might manage
to disguise the Purge's true intention, considering

00:04:29.099 --> 00:04:33.189
the fact that the Experiment is televised,
with a lot of the NFFA's hitmen wearing white

00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:35.669
supremacist garbs in full view.

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:37.009
America first

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:41.379
America might not be quite so beautiful once
the Purge fully takes hold of society, but

00:04:41.379 --> 00:04:45.849
the concept does eventually reduce unemployment
and crime rates by the time the first film

00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:47.370
picks up several years in.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:51.680
In The First Purge, we're treated to a few
news reports about how other First World nations

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.710
like Germany start sanctioning the United
States ahead of the initial Experiment and

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.460
refer to it as "barbaric."

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.410
The question, then, is whether the annual
Purge ever gains steam in other nations as

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.430
a result of its economic impact.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.289
Do those who doubt it eventually decide to
participate themselves, or does the United

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:12.419
States continue to remain isolated and ostracized
by its former allies as a result of its newfound

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:14.240
penchant for practical violence?

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.759
Perhaps the upcoming Purge TV series will
fill in some of these blanks.

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:19.059
Thanks for watching!

